# Web3 AI Wallet — Project Rule

## 1. Product Goal

Build a web-first Web3 wallet with a clean shadcn-style black-and-white UI.

Core wallet capabilities:
- User authentication
- Create/link a wallet
- View wallet address and balances
- Receive assets via address / QR code
- Send native tokens and ERC-20 tokens
- Transaction history
- Payment confirmation
- Smart Account / gas sponsorship where appropriate

Future capabilities:
- AI wallet assistant
- A2A agent integration
- MCP tool integration
- x402 / agent payments
- Merchant and travel-agent integrations
- Automated payment under explicit user-defined policy limits

The product should feel closer to a modern fintech app than a crypto developer dashboard.

---

# 2. Approved Technology Stack

## Frontend
- React
- TypeScript
- Vite
- Tailwind CSS
- shadcn/ui
- TanStack Query
- Zustand
- React Hook Form
- Zod

## Backend
- Hono
- TypeScript

## Web3
- Privy (embedded wallets, social login, external wallets)
- viem for RPC reads, ERC-20 encoding, and gas estimates
- Privy Smart Wallets / gas sponsorship when useful
- x402 when supported by external services

## Database / Auth / Infrastructure
- Supabase
- PostgreSQL
- Supabase Auth
- Supabase RLS
- Supabase Realtime where useful
- Supabase Storage only when needed

## AI / Agents
- OpenAI for reasoning and tool selection
- A2A client for external agent-to-agent integrations
- MCP client for tool integrations

Do not introduce an additional framework or infrastructure dependency unless it solves a real problem that the current stack cannot solve cleanly.

