# 3. Core Architecture

Use the following separation:

User
  ↓
React Web App
  ↓
Hono API / Agent Orchestrator
  ├── Supabase
  ├── OpenAI
  ├── A2A Clients
  ├── MCP Clients
  └── Payment Router
        └── Privy
              ↓
          Blockchain

Responsibilities:

## React
Responsible for:
- UI
- User interaction
- Wallet presentation
- Forms
- Transaction confirmation UI
- AI chat UI
- Local UI state

React must NOT contain:
- Server secrets
- privileged wallet operations
- unrestricted transaction execution
- sensitive policy decisions
- direct database admin access

## Hono
Responsible for:
- API gateway
- authentication verification
- agent orchestration
- A2A calls
- MCP calls
- payment policy checks
- transaction preparation
- payment confirmation
- webhook handling
- idempotency
- server-side Privy / viem operations

## Supabase
Responsible for:
- canonical application user identity
- business data
- wallet mappings
- orders
- agent tasks
- payment requests
- payments
- audit logs

## Privy
Responsible for:
- wallet infrastructure
- key management and signing
- embedded / in-app wallets
- Smart Accounts
- gas sponsorship
- Web3 payment execution where applicable

Privy is NOT the source of truth for application business identity.
x402 facilitators and RPC/indexers are separate providers.

Supabase user ID is the canonical application user ID.

